<BaseLayout
  title="Data Exports | FTFN"
  description="Versioned public JSON exports for FTFN signals, sources, topics, research records, reader pathways, evidence operations, named project conversion files, event ledgers, gate calendars, and stage matrices."
>
  <section class="page-section hero">
    <div class="hero__copy">
      <div class="eyebrow">ftfn.io / Data</div>
      <h1 class="page-title">Inspectable metadata for the evidence stack.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        These static JSON files expose stable public fields without publishing
        private candidate notes, internal automation instructions, or review-only
        signal records.
      </p>
      <div class="meta-row">
        <MetaPill label="Schema 1.0" tone="possibility" />
        <MetaPill label="Static build exports" />
        <MetaPill label="No live API" tone="review" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Datasets</div>
        <h2>Fifty-one bounded public contracts.</h2>
        <p>Each file reports its schema version, dataset name, record scope, count, and records.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="inline-link" href="/method/">Read the publication method</a>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      {datasets.map((dataset) => (
        <article class="record-card">
          <div class="meta-row">
            <MetaPill label={`${dataset.count} records`} tone="possibility" />
            <MetaPill label="JSON" />
          </div>
          <h3><a href={dataset.href}>{dataset.title}</a></h3>
          <p>{dataset.summary}</p>
          <a class="inline-link" href={dataset.href}>Open dataset</a>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section briefing-band">
    <div class="briefing-band__copy">
      <div class="eyebrow">Boundary</div>
      <h2>Exports are publication artifacts, not automated truth.</h2>
      <p>
        The files are regenerated from the reviewed static corpus. They do not
        provide live monitoring, automatic publication, database writes, user
        accounts, or numeric readiness scoring.
      </p>
    </div>
    <article class="record-card">
      <h3>Excluded by design</h3>
      <ul class="compact-list">
        <li>Private source-candidate IDs and registry paths.</li>
        <li>Editorial notes and automation instructions.</li>
        <li>Signals, briefings, maps, and pathways still In Review.</li>
        <li>Claims beyond the source and evidence boundaries.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
